      "writtenOn": "2024-05-13T18:00:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "AndroidAudioStream has a lot of stuff in it, so it is easy for the SAFETY justification to go stale. It is actually already wrong because `Rc` is not thread safe.\n\nInstead I suggest you create a small type to wrap just the `*mut AAudioStream`, e.g. `struct AAudioStreamPtr(*mut AAudioStream);`. Give that type `unsafe impl Send`, but not `unsafe impl Sync` because as the comment above says, `AAudioStream` isn\u0027t thread safe.\n\nThen, you can adjust the rest of the code to make the compiler happy. If `AndroidAudioStream` needs to be `Send` and `Sync`, then you\u0027ll probably want `stream: Arc\u003cMutex\u003cAAudioStreamPtr\u003e\u003e`",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 80,
