      "writtenOn": "2024-05-13T09:22:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for pointing this out.\nI write like this is because of the windows [implementation](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/crosvm/crosvm/+/4878756/comment/f629a15a_30f958ab/).\n\nI didn\u0027t fix it with RefCell because the call flow is like:\n```\n{\n    let stream \u003d AndroidAudioStream::new(/* ... */);\n    let buf \u003d stream.next_playback_buffer.await?;\n    write_audio_data(buf);\n    buf.commit(/* ... */);\n}\n```\nThat cause lifetime and mutable borrow issue.\n\nAnd I finally resolved this by use another struct(`AndroidAudioPlaybackBufferCommit`) instead of `self`\nI\u0027m not sure if it is a good practice.\nDoes this fix make sense to you?",
      "parentUuid": "3d26cc79_d6015b84",
      "revId": "f8bd8609fb9c23842a5b69b92bcfc9789f487286",
